# Re-include the storage package.
#
# A global ignore file (`core.excludesFile`, commonly `~/.gitignore`) with a
# bare `storage/` pattern -- a common entry, aimed at framework or asset
# storage directories -- silently excludes `internal/storage/` here. That is
# how this repository's first commit came to be missing its entire storage
# package while `make check` passed: every gate ran against the working tree,
# where the files are present, and nothing looked at what was actually
# committed. `make check-commit` now does.
#
# Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the
# directory itself has to be un-excluded first.
!internal/storage/
!internal/storage/**
